        <data
            cq:model="/conf/weekender-shared/settings/dam/cfm/models/adventure"
            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured">
            <master
                jcr:mixinTypes="[cq:Taggable,dam:cfVariationNode]"
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                activity="Skiing"
                activity_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.339-07:00"
                adventureType="Overnight Trip"
                adventureType_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.338-07:00"
                description="&lt;p>Around Mont Blanc the lifts stop where the best skiing begins. On skins, with a mountain guide, you reach glaciers and high valleys that most visitors only see from a cable car. We spend three nights in a chalet in the Chamonix valley and one in a mountain hut. You should ski confidently off piste in all kinds of snow and be fit enough to climb a thousand metres in a day; touring experience is useful and not required.&lt;/p>"
                description_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                description_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.337-07:00"
                difficulty="Advanced"
                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.339-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;p>Dress in layers that you can add and remove quickly: you will be hot on the climb and cold at the top within the same half hour.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>Touring skis, bindings, boots and skins&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Avalanche transceiver, shovel and probe&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Harness, ski crampons and helmet&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>A rucksack of 30 to 35 litres&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Thin and thick gloves, goggles and sunglasses&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xa;&lt;p>All of the technical equipment can be hired in the valley; tell us your sizes when you book.&lt;/p>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.341-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}4"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-27T14:50:58.996-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;p>&lt;b>Day 1&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>Arrival at the chalet in the afternoon. The guide checks the equipment, and we practise with transceivers in the garden before dinner.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Day 2&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>A warm-up tour above the valley: 700 metres of climbing, a lesson in kick turns and a descent through larch forest.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Day 3&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>A cable car lifts us to the glacier. We rope up, cross it on skins and climb to a pass on the Italian border, then ski down to the hut for the night.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Day 4&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>The big day. We leave the hut at first light for a summit of 3,500 metres, and ski 2,000 metres of descent back to the valley floor.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>Day 5&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>A short morning tour if the legs and the weather agree, lunch together and departure.&lt;/p>"
                itinerary_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                itinerary_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.340-07:00"
                price="{Double}2600.00"
                price_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:09:50.340-07:00"
